280
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:25,720
Why bring all this up as soon as we meet again?

281
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,560
I was just recklessly brave back then.

282
00:14:28,950 --> 00:14:30,550
Later, a couple

283
00:14:31,390 --> 00:14:32,550
adopted me

284
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,360
and took me to the UK with them.

285
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,976
I'm glad you found people who looked out for you.

286
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:39,847
Enough about that.

287
00:14:39,871 --> 00:14:41,000
Let's eat.

288
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,280
The food's getting cold.

289
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,790
I'm not actually that hungry.

290
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:47,000
I only came here to sit for a while.

291
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,000
That's okay.

292
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:51,870
Just eat what you can.

293
00:15:02,230 --> 00:15:03,046
Full?

294
00:15:03,070 --> 00:15:04,070
If you are, let's go.

295
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,200
Let's go.

296
00:15:07,070 --> 00:15:08,070
I'll pay.

297
00:15:09,150 --> 00:15:10,550
Kid, don't fight me for the bill.

298
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:12,200
Don't be silly.

299
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,256
I ordered the food.

300
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,280
Of course I'm paying.

301
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,950
Foon Gor, wait outside for me.

302
00:15:16,150 --> 00:15:16,790
Sir.

303
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Coming.

304
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,176
How much is it?

305
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,200
One moment.

306
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:27,790
Fei Foon.

307
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:30,990
[May Business Prosper]

308
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:33,096
Calm down and hear me out.

309
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:33,846
About To Si Hong...

310
00:15:33,870 --> 00:15:34,550
What?

311
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:35,630
What do you want to say?

312
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,200
Think carefully.

313
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,150
Your lawyer isn't here now.

314
00:15:39,950 --> 00:15:40,577
With that attitude,

315
00:15:40,601 --> 00:15:41,656
we can't communicate.

316
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:42,790
What attitude?

317
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,736
Unless you tell me who killed To Si Hong,

318
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:48,120
I don't want to hear anything else.

319
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,680
Do you really think I killed him?

320
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:53,520
I don't know.

321
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,230
Right now, I don't even know who you really are.

322
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,736
I know you're angry.

323
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:58,737
I've been looking everywhere for you.

324
00:15:58,761 --> 00:16:00,040
Isn't that enough?

325
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:04,070
Foon Gor.

326
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:06,790
Is this your friend?

327
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
I don't know him.

328
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,120
Let's go.

329
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:14,020
It's you?

330
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,360
Hello, I can't take your call right now.

331
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:32,550
If you...

332
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,336
Loek To, are you ready?

333
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:47,390
We need to get going.

334
00:16:59,550 --> 00:17:00,550
Let's go.

335
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:05,686
[Bayfront Metropolis Construction] Now, the highlight of the event.

336
00:17:05,710 --> 00:17:08,576
[Phase One Launching Ceremony] Tin Ping Group previously commissioned.

337
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,256
Stanley University to conduct a comprehensive

338
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,680
environmental assessment of the Bayfront Metropolis project.

339
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,096
It received the highest rating, Grade A,

340
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:16,686
meaning the project can now proceed

341
00:17:16,710 --> 00:17:18,230
with preliminary work for phase one.

342
00:17:18,390 --> 00:17:19,446
Today, we are honoured to have

343
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:20,896
the Director of Environmental Protection,

344
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,336
Mr. Wong Tak Kuen,

345
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:23,057
join us

346
00:17:23,081 --> 00:17:25,870
at this simple yet formal launching ceremony.

347
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:26,687
Ready?

348
00:17:26,711 --> 00:17:28,256
- Three, two...
- Get out of my way!

349
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:29,656
Hui Loek To, you hypocrite!

350
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,680
You're a fraud!

351
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:32,337
Do you know

352
00:17:32,361 --> 00:17:33,976
the funding for Tin Ping Group's landscaping project

353
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,230
is all dirty money?

354
00:17:35,310 --> 00:17:36,366
Because I found out,

355
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:37,686
you had people beat me up

356
00:17:37,710 --> 00:17:38,846
and hold me against my will.

357
00:17:38,870 --> 00:17:39,910
He pretends to be a saint,

358
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:41,007
doing charity everywhere.

359
00:17:41,031 --> 00:17:42,336
But in fact, it's all an act!

360
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,896
He paints himself as an honest businessman,

361
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,550
but he's really a gangster!

362
00:17:46,950 --> 00:17:47,497
Out of my way!

363
00:17:47,521 --> 00:17:49,126
Sir, I'd like to ask you something.

364
00:17:49,150 --> 00:17:50,206
Do you have evidence

365
00:17:50,230 --> 00:17:52,360
that Mr. Hui Loek To had you severely beaten?

366
00:17:52,630 --> 00:17:53,527
And as for your claim

367
00:17:53,551 --> 00:17:55,446
that Tin Ping Group's project is funded with dirty money,

368
00:17:55,470 --> 00:17:57,080
do you have any concrete evidence?

369
00:17:57,390 --> 00:17:59,056
Mr. Hui, do you know this man?

370
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,446
Is what he's saying true?

371
00:18:00,470 --> 00:18:02,926
Is this project funded entirely with dirty money?

372
00:18:02,950 --> 00:18:05,206
Do you secretly run illegal businesses linked to organised crime?

373
00:18:05,230 --> 00:18:06,550
Please respond. Thank you.

374
00:18:06,630 --> 00:18:07,686
Chairman Hui, regarding these allegations,

375
00:18:07,710 --> 00:18:09,030
do you have anything to say?

376
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:10,230
Let go of me!

377
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:11,520
Hui Loek To!

378
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:13,736
I'm settling this with you today!

379
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,760
Stay out of this!

380
00:18:19,710 --> 00:18:20,846
Avoiding the questions won't solve anything,

381
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:21,310
Mr. Hui.

382
00:18:21,630 --> 00:18:22,446
Everyone saw that!

383
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:23,470
He assaulted me!

384
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,446
His brother is in on it with him.

385
00:18:25,470 --> 00:18:26,840
They're both gangsters!

386
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:28,526
I'm calling the police.

387
00:18:28,550 --> 00:18:30,056
I'm going to sue the whole Hui family.

388
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,720
I'll sue them until they lose everything!

389
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:35,440
[Sham Shui Po Police Station]

390
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:39,846
If you won't cooperate, you can keep sitting there.

391
00:18:39,870 --> 00:18:42,950
You can't leave until the 48 hours are up.

392
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:48,080
On.

393
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:50,710
That man is a real handful.

394
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:51,847
What happened?

395
00:18:51,871 --> 00:18:53,606
He barged into Tin Ping Group's event and accused

396
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:54,846
the chairman of involvement in organised crime,

397
00:18:54,870 --> 00:18:56,360
false imprisonment and assault.

398
00:18:56,470 --> 00:18:57,446
But once he got to the station,

399
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:58,336
he wouldn't say a word.

400
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:59,446
He wouldn't get a lawyer either.

401
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:01,096
He refuses to talk unless the media are around,

402
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:02,520
like we're the ones out to get him.

403
00:19:02,950 --> 00:19:04,360
What exactly is he trying to do?

404
00:19:04,390 --> 00:19:05,760
Is he only after media attention?

405
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,550
Who knows? Either way, he's a real headache.

406
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,446
The younger Mr. Hui, however,

407
00:19:10,470 --> 00:19:12,390
has been surprisingly cooperative.

408
00:19:12,470 --> 00:19:13,550
He answered every question.

409
00:19:15,230 --> 00:19:16,440
That's unexpected.

410
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:18,200
I'll get back to work.

411
00:19:34,790 --> 00:19:35,446
Mr. Hui,

412
00:19:35,470 --> 00:19:36,286
please wait here

413
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:37,496
while I finish the formalities.

414
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:38,630
Mr. Choi, this way, please.

415
00:19:59,630 --> 00:20:03,230
You're Hui Loek To's younger brother, Hui Luk King, right?

416
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,120
Yes. Hello,

417
00:20:05,950 --> 00:20:06,950
Officer Mok.

418
00:20:08,030 --> 00:20:12,120
I heard you pushed Mr. Wong off the stage this afternoon

419
00:20:12,310 --> 00:20:13,286
and injured him.

420
00:20:13,310 --> 00:20:14,310
Is that true?

421
00:20:15,230 --> 00:20:17,440
It was chaotic at the time.

422
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:21,280
I was worried he'd hurt my brother,

423
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:23,846
so I stepped in to separate them

424
00:20:23,870 --> 00:20:25,550
and accidentally pushed him to the ground.

425
00:20:26,470 --> 00:20:28,120
Is he all right?

426
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:30,096
You really are brothers.

427
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,120
You're both great actors.

428
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:33,230
You know my brother?

429
00:20:34,870 --> 00:20:36,950
I don't know if I really know him.

430
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:39,520
Anyway, the Hui family

431
00:20:39,630 --> 00:20:42,790
are legitimate business people at Tin Ping Group on the surface,

432
00:20:43,630 --> 00:20:46,120
but behind the scenes, you run the shady Sheng Tung.

433
00:20:46,630 --> 00:20:47,870
Tell me the truth.

434
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:51,230
What other illegal things has your brother been involved in?

435
00:20:54,950 --> 00:20:58,360
You're the officer who's been giving my brother such a hard time.

436
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:00,390
He.

437
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,230
Mentioned me to you?

438
00:21:02,630 --> 00:21:03,470
No.

439
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:06,000
I heard about you from Fung.

440
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:10,417
I'm glad you're here.

441
00:21:10,441 --> 00:21:12,001
There's something I wanted to tell you.

442
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:14,790
Go ahead.

443
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:17,550
Officer Mok,

444
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:21,080
I think you know our family background is fairly complicated.

445
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:23,440
Ever since our father passed away,

446
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:26,360
my brother had to learn how to take over the family businesses,

447
00:21:27,150 --> 00:21:28,336
what he should do,

448
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,080
what he shouldn't do,

449
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:31,816
and how to negotiate with people

450
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:33,600
without revealing what he really thought.

451
00:21:35,150 --> 00:21:36,336
At the end of the day,

452
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:37,366
the more you say,

453
00:21:37,390 --> 00:21:38,816
the more likely you are to expose your weaknesses.

454
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:40,550
What does any of that have to do with me?

455
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,896
Fung told me that at the casino last time,

456
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:46,760
my brother had countless chances to get out clean

457
00:21:46,870 --> 00:21:48,416
and keep everything hidden from you,

458
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:51,080
but he chose not to.

459
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,336
So because he saved me,

460
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:56,200
I'm supposed to accept his grey-area dealings,

461
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:58,120
the fact that he hides things from me,

462
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:00,230
and all the illegal things he does?

463
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:02,790
What I'm saying is,

464
00:22:03,550 --> 00:22:05,440
after you came into his life,

465
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:09,000
he no longer cared only about the family's interests.

466
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:11,790
He doesn't even put his own safety first anymore.

467
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,000
Actually,

468
00:22:17,390 --> 00:22:18,576
whether you forgive him or not

469
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:19,686
isn't for me to interfere with.

470
00:22:19,710 --> 00:22:20,790
It's just

471
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:24,150
that no one in our world has complete freedom of choice,

472
00:22:24,310 --> 00:22:25,520
especially not my brother.

473
00:22:25,630 --> 00:22:26,790
He's in a position

474
00:22:27,310 --> 00:22:29,080
of great responsibility.

475
00:22:29,310 --> 00:22:30,310
There are many things

476
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:32,240
he simply can't decide for himself.

477
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,760
What kind of responsibility has to be shouldered

478
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:37,200
through shady dealings and illegal business?

479
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:38,520
Seriously?

480
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:41,230
Are you telling me how tough it is to be rich right now?

481
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:42,840
Officer Mok,

482
00:22:42,950 --> 00:22:44,816
haven't you ever had to make

483
00:22:44,840 --> 00:22:46,576
a difficult choice because of your job?

484
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:47,680
What do you mean by that?

485
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:49,840
Are you saying I'd break the law too?

486
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:52,920
No, that's not what I mean.

487
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:56,120
I'm just trying to tell you

488
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:57,600
that my brother

489
00:22:57,840 --> 00:23:00,550
only shows people what he wants them to see.

490
00:23:00,950 --> 00:23:02,630
He's like that even with me.

491
00:23:02,790 --> 00:23:05,600
Maybe it's because he's guarded,

492
00:23:05,870 --> 00:23:07,750
or maybe he doesn't want to cause more trouble.

493
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:12,950
Only he knows the real reason.

494
00:23:16,710 --> 00:23:18,230
I know he's under pressure.

495
00:23:19,550 --> 00:23:21,110
But no matter how little choice he has,

496
00:23:22,470 --> 00:23:24,710
at the very least, he should be honest with me.

497
00:23:26,470 --> 00:23:27,790
Honest?

498
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,526
Asking him to be honest

499
00:23:30,550 --> 00:23:33,510
is like making him abandon what he's relied on to survive all these years.

500
00:23:33,710 --> 00:23:35,190
The consequences could be even worse.

501
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:36,127
But I can't stand

502
00:23:36,151 --> 00:23:38,191
being with someone who always hides things from me.

503
00:23:39,310 --> 00:23:39,927
I understand.

504
00:23:39,951 --> 00:23:41,710
That's up to you.

505
00:23:42,710 --> 00:23:43,710
But

506
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:47,520
as much as I worry that my brother

507
00:23:47,550 --> 00:23:49,550
will act without regard for his own safety,

508
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:50,870
I haven't

509
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:54,006
seen him smile so genuinely

510
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:56,550
in a very long time.

511
00:23:59,130 --> 00:24:00,130
Anyway,

512
00:24:00,740 --> 00:24:02,370
while he may seem successful

513
00:24:02,660 --> 00:24:04,500
and capable of anything in the business world,

514
00:24:05,100 --> 00:24:07,340
getting him to open up

515
00:24:07,370 --> 00:24:09,100
and say what he really feels is

516
00:24:09,310 --> 00:24:10,710
something I can't begin to imagine.

517
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:12,950
Why don't I leave that to you?

518
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:15,126
Sit him down and make him have a proper talk with you.

519
00:24:15,150 --> 00:24:17,390
Maybe he'll be willing to open up to you.

520
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:19,950
You think I want a talk with him?

521
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:22,000
What he thinks has nothing to do with me.

522
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:24,847
All right, Officer Mok.

523
00:24:24,871 --> 00:24:26,030
Whatever you say.

524
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:31,150
Officer Mok, what are you doing here?

525
00:24:31,310 --> 00:24:32,000
Well,

526
00:24:32,120 --> 00:24:33,200
I had a few words with him.

527
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:39,950
Mr. Hui,

528
00:24:40,150 --> 00:24:41,606
all the paperwork has been completed.

529
00:24:41,630 --> 00:24:42,630
You may leave now.

530
00:25:07,550 --> 00:25:08,550
Siu Kit.

531
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:10,680
Do you have Hui Loek To's file ready?

532
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:12,710
It's right here.

533
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:14,200
Give me a moment.

534
00:25:17,790 --> 00:25:18,790
Here's everything.

535
00:25:20,780 --> 00:25:23,260
[Property Tycoon Shot Dead in Suspected Gang Dispute]

536
00:25:23,290 --> 00:25:25,370
[Gang Infighting: Leader Likely Killed by Associate]

537
00:25:26,950 --> 00:25:28,000
That's it?

538
00:25:28,950 --> 00:25:30,760
Wasn't Sheng Tung a fairly large operation?

539
00:25:31,080 --> 00:25:32,080
That's it.

540
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:34,710
Sheng Tung was built up by two elders of the Hui family.

541
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:36,400
They were powerful in the early days.

542
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:37,950
But after an internal power struggle,

543
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:40,896
Old Mr. Hui was ousted and stripped of power by Sheng Tung's senior members,

544
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:42,176
and Sheng Tung declined sharply.

545
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:45,000
His two sons don't have much influence now.

546
00:25:48,790 --> 00:25:49,576
Thanks.

547
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,286
No problem.

548
00:25:50,310 --> 00:25:51,310
I'll get back to work.

549
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:12,680
[Do you have time to meet?]

550
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:21,626
[Police Station]

551
00:26:21,650 --> 00:26:23,200
[Sham Shui Po Police Station]

552
00:26:23,230 --> 00:26:26,120
The police didn't give you a hard time, did they?

553
00:26:26,550 --> 00:26:27,336
No.

554
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:28,480
They just took my statement.

555
00:26:28,950 --> 00:26:31,750
I heard from an officer that Mr. Wong isn't planning to press charges.

556
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:33,440
That's unusual.

557
00:26:34,230 --> 00:26:36,126
I'll have Fung look into why he suddenly came to cause trouble

558
00:26:36,150 --> 00:26:37,630
and then backed off just as suddenly.

559
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,310
Has Director Wong said anything?

560
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:42,550
Director Wong

561
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:46,030
now has concerns about Tin Ping Group.

562
00:26:46,790 --> 00:26:49,126
The environmental assessment report will have to wait until the police

563
00:26:49,150 --> 00:26:50,336
complete their investigation

564
00:26:50,360 --> 00:26:52,200
before it can proceed as originally planned.

565
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:53,920
It can't be expedited.

566
00:26:55,550 --> 00:26:57,950
So how long will the Bayfront Metropolis project be delayed?

567
00:26:58,310 --> 00:27:00,350
That depends on how quickly the investigation goes.

568
00:27:02,950 --> 00:27:04,310
What's wrong? Are you okay?

569
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:07,926
The investors said they needed

570
00:27:07,950 --> 00:27:09,896
to reassess whether they still wanted to invest.

571
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:10,920
What should we do?

572
00:27:11,390 --> 00:27:12,600
That's nothing major.

573
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:15,446
Your top priority now is to get some rest.

574
00:27:15,470 --> 00:27:17,030
Deal with tomorrow's problems tomorrow.

575
00:27:17,710 --> 00:27:18,446
Okay?

576
00:27:18,470 --> 00:27:19,287
Okay.

577
00:27:19,311 --> 00:27:20,336
The car's up ahead.

578
00:27:20,360 --> 00:27:21,360
Let's go.

579
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:31,920
[Do you have time to meet?]

580
00:27:35,390 --> 00:27:36,176
Something came up.

581
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:37,200
You go back first.

582
00:27:37,230 --> 00:27:38,230
Drive.

583
00:27:58,230 --> 00:27:59,230
Fei Foon.

584
00:28:14,790 --> 00:28:16,670
I had nothing to do with the counterfeit notes.

585
00:28:19,310 --> 00:28:20,950
I didn't send anyone to beat up Mr. Wong.

586
00:28:22,390 --> 00:28:23,760
I didn't kill To Si Hong.

587
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:28,310
I don't care what the rumours say.

588
00:28:29,150 --> 00:28:30,520
If I didn't do it, I didn't do it.

589
00:28:35,630 --> 00:28:38,950
Why didn't you ever tell me about your organised crime background?

590
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:45,630
Are you trying to turn Tin Ping into a criminal organisation?

591
00:28:47,310 --> 00:28:48,310
Of course not.

592
00:28:49,230 --> 00:28:51,440
Then why are you involved with those people?

593
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:54,710
Doesn't the police force

594
00:28:55,760 --> 00:28:57,120
have a file on Sheng Tung?

595
00:28:58,440 --> 00:28:59,710
I want to hear it from you.

596
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:23,710
Can you play basketball?

597
00:29:24,550 --> 00:29:25,550
I can, a little.

598
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:27,390
Let's make a bet.

599
00:29:28,120 --> 00:29:29,310
Teach me how to play.

600
00:29:29,950 --> 00:29:32,896
If I can make a three-pointer tonight,

601
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:34,160
I won't ask any more questions.

602
00:29:34,790 --> 00:29:37,030
But if I don't make a single one all night,

603
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:38,256
you have to tell me the truth

604
00:29:38,280 --> 00:29:39,976
about why you're involved with those people.

605
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Deal?

606
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,686
A three-pointer's too hard.

607
00:29:42,710 --> 00:29:43,710
Make it a free throw.

608
00:29:43,950 --> 00:29:45,030
Are you teaching me or not?

609
00:29:45,470 --> 00:29:46,470
Come on.

610
00:29:51,870 --> 00:29:52,870
Here.

611
00:30:14,630 --> 00:30:15,630
Look.

612
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:18,030
Shooting is easy.

613
00:30:18,440 --> 00:30:20,176
"Your left hand is only there to guide the ball."

614
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:21,200
Ever heard that before?

615
00:30:22,030 --> 00:30:23,470
Shoot it like this.

616
00:30:24,710 --> 00:30:25,710
You try.

617
00:30:28,030 --> 00:30:28,847
Like this.

618
00:30:28,871 --> 00:30:29,920
Hold the ball properly.

619
00:30:31,630 --> 00:30:32,630
That's it.

620
00:30:33,120 --> 00:30:34,150
Grip it from above.

621
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:36,520
Push with your middle finger.

622
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Raise it up

623
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:41,630
and release from here.

624
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,320
Let's put the ball down first.

625
00:30:45,950 --> 00:30:46,950
Feet apart.

626
00:30:48,310 --> 00:30:48,817
That's right.

627
00:30:48,841 --> 00:30:50,001
Now bend your knees slightly.

628
00:30:51,630 --> 00:30:52,607
When I say, "Ready, three, two, one,"

629
00:30:52,631 --> 00:30:53,680
shoot the ball upwards.

630
00:30:54,630 --> 00:30:55,607
All right. Ready?

631
00:30:55,631 --> 00:30:57,550
Three, two, one.

632
00:31:04,630 --> 00:31:05,910
- Go get the ball.
- You get it.

633
00:31:42,760 --> 00:31:44,080
Do you think this one will go in?

634
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:45,280
Yeah.

635
00:31:52,150 --> 00:31:53,310
Normally, I'd make that shot.

636
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:54,920
Get the ball for me.

637
00:31:55,550 --> 00:31:56,550
I'm not getting it.

638
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:06,840
So,

639
00:32:07,630 --> 00:32:09,190
why are you involved in shady dealings?

640
00:32:09,470 --> 00:32:10,470
Does it really matter?

641
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:12,470
If it didn't, I wouldn't keep asking.

642
00:32:16,390 --> 00:32:17,870
It goes back a long way.

643
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:22,760
Both my parents started out as gangsters.

644
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:27,120
They founded Tin Ping only to go legit.

645
00:32:28,470 --> 00:32:30,590
A lot of the older generation got involved back then,

646
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:33,950
and those ties have carried on to this day.

647
00:32:37,030 --> 00:32:38,840
Can't you just pay them to leave?

648
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:40,840
They're all in it for the money anyway.

649
00:32:41,280 --> 00:32:42,520
It's not that simple.

650
00:32:43,120 --> 00:32:44,360
Have you tried?

651
00:32:55,470 --> 00:32:56,680
My dad did.

652
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:00,920
Hui,

653
00:33:01,790 --> 00:33:03,200
now that you've made it,

654
00:33:03,870 --> 00:33:06,080
you don't care what happens to us anymore, do you?

655
00:33:06,600 --> 00:33:08,160
I've warned you many times.

656
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:10,350
Your materials and workmanship

657
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:11,710
are substandard,

658
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:13,520
and your contractor isn't honest either.

659
00:33:13,990 --> 00:33:16,006
The fact that I waited this long to change contractors

660
00:33:16,030 --> 00:33:17,256
is already doing you a favour.

661
00:33:17,280 --> 00:33:18,840
You just want to destroy my livelihood!

662
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,080
Save your excuses!

663
00:33:20,390 --> 00:33:21,510
Times have changed.

664
00:33:22,190 --> 00:33:23,616
When you run a legitimate business,

665
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:26,120
people expect you to deal fairly with everyone.

666
00:33:26,390 --> 00:33:27,640
You can't just force a deal.

667
00:33:28,280 --> 00:33:29,800
If you can't adapt to the times,

668
00:33:30,030 --> 00:33:31,910
you'd better find another way to make a living.

669
00:33:38,510 --> 00:33:39,510
Hui!

670
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:45,526
You made a bit of money in real estate, and now you think you're something?

671
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:46,550
Listen carefully.

672
00:33:46,870 --> 00:33:49,710
If we hadn't risked our lives for the gang,

673
00:33:49,830 --> 00:33:51,096
would you be where you are today?

674
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:52,120
As long as you're alive,

675
00:33:52,190 --> 00:33:54,080
you're not leaving us behind!

676
00:33:55,030 --> 00:33:56,160
Don't even think about it!

677
00:33:57,120 --> 00:33:58,480
Don't you dare!

678
00:34:02,550 --> 00:34:03,670
Drop dead!

679
00:34:06,090 --> 00:34:09,540
I watched my dad die right in front of me.

680
00:34:14,440 --> 00:34:16,440
Don't look at me like that.

681
00:34:19,670 --> 00:34:22,510
In fact, my mum has always been loyal to her people.

682
00:34:23,390 --> 00:34:26,550
After all, she and those old friends have been through life and death together.

683
00:34:30,350 --> 00:34:32,870
All I can do is turn a blind eye.

684
00:34:34,190 --> 00:34:35,510
As long as they make their money,

685
00:34:36,830 --> 00:34:37,896
stay out of trouble,

686
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:39,720
and don't interfere with Tin Ping's business,

687
00:34:39,830 --> 00:34:41,870
I pretend nothing's happening.

688
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:45,640
How much does your brother know?

689
00:34:46,160 --> 00:34:47,846
My brother was still young back then.

690
00:34:47,870 --> 00:34:48,870
He doesn't remember much.

691
00:34:55,480 --> 00:34:57,190
Once the older generation is gone,

692
00:34:57,640 --> 00:34:59,080
I won't have my hands tied anymore.

693
00:35:06,230 --> 00:35:07,230
Okay.

694
00:35:08,990 --> 00:35:09,990
Okay?

695
00:35:13,030 --> 00:35:14,030
Okay.

696
00:35:23,350 --> 00:35:24,350
Actually,

697
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:26,240
the way you're feeling right now

698
00:35:26,990 --> 00:35:29,590
is exactly how I felt when I found out you were a police officer.

699
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:30,577
What?

700
00:35:30,601 --> 00:35:32,166
Are you raking up the past now?

701
00:35:32,190 --> 00:35:33,670
I'm saying I know how you feel.

702
00:35:35,030 --> 00:35:36,030
Happy now?

703
00:35:40,190 --> 00:35:43,280
From now on, you have to tell me if anything happens.

704
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:45,160
Stop hiding things from me.

705
00:35:45,670 --> 00:35:46,670
Can you do that?

706
00:35:55,350 --> 00:35:56,350
Got it.

707
00:36:18,160 --> 00:36:19,160
Hey, sirs.

708
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:20,320
We're closing up.

709
00:36:24,230 --> 00:36:25,230
Our clothes!

710
00:36:56,290 --> 00:37:04,290
[Episode 4] [This story is fictional. Any resemblance is entirely coincidental.]
